                                    <h1>Jewelry Google Ads — Search + Shopping + PMax Playbook 2026 | ITD GrowthLabs</h1>
                                    <div style="background:#fff7ed;border-left:4px solid #ff5722;padding:20px 24px;border-radius:10px;margin:24px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#334155;"><strong style="color:#ea580c;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:0.4px;">ITD JEWELRY PORTFOLIO &mdash; THE EVIDENCE:</strong><br>This article is written from live jewelry vertical work. ITD GrowthLabs is a specialist <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-jewelry-brands.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">digital marketing agency for jewelry brands</a> with a delivered <a href="/resources/Fabelia_Jewelry_D2C_Marketing_Strategy_Case_Study_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Fabelia jewelry D2C case study</a>, 8+ published jewelry playbooks including <a href="/resources/Gold_vs_Diamond_Jewelry_D2C_Strategy_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Gold vs Diamond D2C Strategy</a>, <a href="/resources/Jewelry_D2C_Digital_Transformation_India_Dubai_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Jewelry D2C Digital Transformation India + Dubai</a>, <a href="/resources/Best_D2C_Jewellery_Brands_UAE_GCC_2026_2027.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Best D2C Jewellery Brands UAE + GCC</a>, and city-specific jewelry marketing pages across <a href="/services/gcc/dubai-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Dubai</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/abu-dhabi-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Abu Dhabi</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/jeddah-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Jeddah</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/doha-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Doha</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/dammam-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Dammam</a>, and <a href="/services/gcc/al-khobar-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Al Khobar</a>. Every framework below is grounded in live category work &mdash; not generic D2C theory.</div><p>Google Ads is the highest-intent paid channel for D2C jewelry brands. Buyers searching "lab-grown diamond engagement ring under 3 lakh" are literally 24-72 hours from purchasing. Capturing them requires proper Search + Shopping + Performance Max structure &mdash; not a generic e-com playbook.</p><p>This is the Google Ads structure we deploy for D2C jewelry clients &mdash; campaign architecture, keyword strategy, Shopping feed spec, PMax setup, and CPL benchmarks.</p>
                                    <h2>Campaign architecture &amp;mdash; one per (category x intent)</h2>
                                    <p>The wrong way: one campaign called "Jewelry", all keywords, single budget. The right way: one campaign per (category x intent) combination.</p><p><strong>Example structure for fine + fashion hybrid brand:</strong></p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Campaign: Search &mdash; Engagement rings. Ad groups: lab-grown, mined, solitaire, halo. Budget Rs 40K/mo.</li><li>Campaign: Search &mdash; Fashion rings. Ad groups: minimalist, statement, cocktail, everyday. Budget Rs 25K/mo.</li><li>Campaign: Search &mdash; Earrings. Ad groups by style. Budget Rs 20K/mo.</li><li>Campaign: Search &mdash; Necklaces + pendants. Budget Rs 20K/mo.</li><li>Campaign: Shopping &mdash; Fine jewelry feed. Budget Rs 60K/mo.</li><li>Campaign: Shopping &mdash; Fashion jewelry feed. Budget Rs 35K/mo.</li><li>Campaign: Performance Max &mdash; Site retargeting + lookalike. Budget Rs 40K/mo.</li><li>Campaign: Brand terms. Small budget (Rs 5-10K/mo) to defend brand search.</li></ul><p>This granular structure lets you control budget by category profitability, CPL by intent tier, and creative-audience match. Overhead is higher than single-campaign but pays back within week 2-3.</p>
                                    <h2>Keyword strategy by intent tier</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Transactional (Rs 350-1,500 CPL, highest priority):</strong></p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>"[metal] [piece] under [budget]" &mdash; "22k gold chain under 50k"</li><li>"[gemstone] [piece] for [occasion]" &mdash; "diamond ring for engagement"</li><li>"buy [piece] online india" &mdash; "buy solitaire ring online india"</li><li>"[brand] alternatives" &mdash; brand-adjacent capture</li></ul><p><strong>Comparison (Rs 400-1,000 CPL, medium priority):</strong></p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>"[your brand] vs [competitor]"</li><li>"lab-grown vs mined diamond"</li><li>"22k vs 18k gold jewelry"</li></ul><p><strong>Informational (low paid priority, high SEO priority):</strong></p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>"how to choose engagement ring"</li><li>"diamond 4Cs explained"</li><li>"jewelry care tips"</li></ul><p>Match types: exact + phrase for transactional. Broad match modifier for comparison. Broad match with tight negative lists only after 30 days of baseline data + Smart Bidding.</p>
                                    <h2>Shopping feed &amp;mdash; the compound ROI channel</h2>
                                    <p>Google Shopping is the highest-ROI paid channel for jewelry D2C over 12 months. Feed setup essentials:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Product feed via Merchant Center:</strong> Every SKU with title + description + price + image + brand + GTIN (if applicable) + condition + availability + shipping.</li><li><strong>Jewelry-specific attributes:</strong> product_type (Rings > Engagement > Solitaire), material (22k gold), color (yellow gold), size (7), gemstone (diamond, 1ct), certification (BIS + HUID + GIA).</li><li><strong>Title optimisation:</strong> [Brand] [Metal] [Piece] [Style] [Gemstone] [Weight] &mdash; "Fabelia 22k Gold Solitaire Engagement Ring Diamond 0.5ct". First 30 characters critical &mdash; that's the mobile crop.</li><li><strong>Image quality:</strong> 800x800px minimum. White background hero. Additional angles allowed. AR-ready 3D thumbnail lifts CTR 15-25%.</li><li><strong>Custom labels:</strong> Tag SKUs by margin tier, seasonality, best-seller status. Bid separately.</li><li><strong>Feed hygiene:</strong> Monthly audit. Drop out-of-stock. Refresh titles for new collections. Add new SKUs within 48 hours of launch.</li></ul><p>Well-structured Shopping feed delivers 3-5x lower CPL than Search for the same buyer intent + scales more efficiently.</p>
                                    <h2>Performance Max &amp;mdash; where + how to use it</h2>
                                    <p>PMax works for jewelry when configured right. Common failure: launching PMax without conversion history + expecting Google to figure it out. Result: 40-60% ad spend waste on low-intent inventory.</p><p><strong>PMax jewelry recipe:</strong></p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Wait until you have 30+ conversions logged in Google Ads + Merchant Center.</li><li>Deploy enhanced conversions + Conversion API + offline conversion imports.</li><li>Feed 8-15 high-quality creative asset groups (image + video + headline + description variations).</li><li>Audience signals: past converters (customer email upload) + high-LTV lookalikes + Meta Pixel + Conversion API visitors.</li><li>Budget shape: 25-40% of paid budget on PMax after baseline established.</li><li>Exclusion list: brand search terms (don't compete with your own brand campaign) + irrelevant categories.</li></ul><p>Well-configured PMax generates 15-30% additional conversions at CPL comparable to Search + 30% lower than cold Display.</p>
                                    <h2>CPL benchmarks + what to expect</h2>
                                    <p>Directional jewelry Google Ads CPL benchmarks (India, mid-2026):</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Search &mdash; fashion jewelry:</strong> Rs 60-250 CPL</li><li><strong>Search &mdash; fine jewelry (transactional):</strong> Rs 350-1,500 CPL</li><li><strong>Search &mdash; bridal + wedding:</strong> Rs 800-3,500 CPL</li><li><strong>Search &mdash; lab-grown diamond:</strong> Rs 400-1,200 CPL</li><li><strong>Shopping &mdash; all categories:</strong> 3-5x lower CPL than Search for same intent</li><li><strong>PMax:</strong> Rs 250-800 CPL when properly configured (after 30+ conversions baseline)</li><li><strong>Brand campaign:</strong> Rs 40-150 CPL &mdash; near-100% conversion for brand-search intent</li></ul><p>These are directional. SQL cost (CRM-verified qualified pipeline) is 2-3x CPL and the metric that matters for the P&L.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
                                        <h3 style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:15px;">Ready to Get Started?</h3>
                                        <p style="color:#ccc;margin-bottom:25px;">Book a free 30-minute jewelry D2C discovery call. We map your brand + funnel + share a customised proposal within 3 working days.</p>
                                        <a href="https://www.itdgrowthlabs.com/contact-us.php" style="background:#ff5722;color:#fff;padding:14px 32px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block;margin-right:10px;">Contact Us Today</a>
                                        <a href="https://calendly.com/itdgrowthlabs-info/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="js-book-call" data-source="blog_cta" style="background:#1565c0;color:#fff;padding:14px 32px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block;">Book Free 30-min Call</a>
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is a realistic Google Ads budget for a D2C jewelry brand?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 60K-Rs 1.5 lakh / month for founder-led boutique. Rs 2-6 lakh / month for mid-market. Rs 6-20 lakh+ / month for enterprise. Ad spend on top of retainer. Budget shape: 40% Search + 35% Shopping + 20% PMax + 5% Brand defence.</p>
                                        <h3>Should jewelry brands use Google Shopping or Search Ads first?</h3>
                                        <p>Search Ads first for fine + bridal + high-consideration (needs keyword control). Shopping Ads first for fashion jewelry (visual-driven + broader intent capture). Ideally both in parallel with proper feed hygiene after 30-day baseline.</p>
                                        <h3>How do we structure Google Shopping feed for jewelry?</h3>
                                        <p>Product feed via Merchant Center with jewelry-specific attributes (material, gemstone, weight, certification), optimised titles ([Brand] [Metal] [Piece] [Style] [Gemstone] [Weight]), 800x800px+ hero images, custom labels by margin tier, monthly feed hygiene. Add new SKUs within 48 hours of launch.</p>
                                        <h3>When should we use Performance Max for jewelry?</h3>
                                        <p>After 30+ conversions logged in Google Ads. Deploy enhanced conversions + Conversion API + offline conversion imports. Feed 8-15 creative asset groups. Audience signals: past converters + LTV lookalikes. 25-40% of paid budget on PMax after baseline. Generates 15-30% additional conversions.</p>
                                        <h3>What CPL should we expect on Google Ads for jewelry?</h3>
                                        <p>Fashion jewelry Rs 60-250. Fine jewelry transactional Rs 350-1,500. Bridal + wedding Rs 800-3,500. Lab-grown diamond Rs 400-1,200. Shopping 3-5x lower CPL than Search. Brand campaign Rs 40-150 (near-100% conversion). SQL cost 2-3x CPL and is the number that matters for P&L.</p>
                                        <h3>How do we prevent Google Ads waste on generic clicks?</h3>
                                        <p>Comprehensive negative-keyword library (avoid "free", "cheap", "fake", "how to make", brand-competitor terms unless intentional). Phrase / exact match instead of broad initially. Granular ad-group structure. Landing-page-quality-driven Quality Score. Typical waste reduction 25-45% by week 4.</p>
                                        <h3>Do we need dedicated landing pages for jewelry Google Ads?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes. Dedicated landing page per campaign matching search intent. H1 matches query + ad copy. Above-fold price + gemstone + BIS/HUID + WhatsApp CTA + 360&deg; view. Landing-page-quality-driven Quality Score can reduce CPL 20-40%.</p>
                                        <h3>How does ITD GrowthLabs manage jewelry Google Ads?</h3>
                                        <p>Campaign architecture + keyword research + negative-keyword library + Shopping feed + PMax setup + landing pages + weekly optimisation + monthly QBR + CRM-attributed reporting. Rs 8Cr+ annual managed spend across 100+ D2C accounts including jewelry. See our <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-jewelry-brands.php">jewelry vertical page</a>.</p>
